{"id":"refine_20260929132019605","summary":"Updated the global task-76e8f616 memory to preserve the demonstrated suffix-fill rule while warning against applying it without identifying the qualifying row pattern.","rationale":"The demonstrations consistently recolor a trailing background suffix to 1 after a foreground run, while complete rows remain unchanged. Some demos involve repeated or noisy row motifs, and all submissions on the presented test failed, so the evidence does not justify a blanket rule for every internal run.","expectedOutcome":"Future solvers should retain the demonstrated transformation but first use row or panel structure to determine which suffixes qualify; validate against all demo pairs and avoid indiscriminate suffix conversion.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_76e8f616_extend_incomplete_horizontal_runs_to_right_edge","title":"ARC task-76e8f616: extend qualifying incomplete horizontal runs to the right edge","content":"For task-76e8f616, demonstrations show that a qualifying horizontal foreground run followed by a trailing suffix of the row's background is extended to the right edge by recoloring that suffix to color 1; preserve the foreground run and leave complete rows unchanged. Confirmed examples include a color-7 run on background 6, a color-2 run on background 4 with one trailing background cell, and a color-7 run on background 0. Other demos show multiple changed rows amid repeated or noisy motifs. Do not apply this transformation indiscriminately to every row containing an internal foreground run followed by background. First infer which rows qualify from the panel, repetition, or row-motif structure; demos alone do not establish a simple run-only condition. A test instance with mixed prefixes and motifs remained unresolved after several unsuccessful submissions, so avoid treating that outcome as validation of a particular selection rule.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Adds cross-demo evide