al noise pixels when identifying the dominant signal. Validated test output for the 9×9 input was [[6,2,7],[8,0,0],[8,0,0]]. A demo confirmed that a tile containing signal color 4 outputs 4, a solid 8 tile outputs 8, and tiles with no signal output 0. Key lesson: do not include background color 5 in the vote.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:06:15.808Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:08:15.449Z","version":2},"after":{"id":"arc_task_dd6a9489_decode_signal_colors_from_noisy_tiles","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-dd6a9489: decode colors independently from aligned 3×3 tiles","content":"For task-dd6a9489, partition the input into aligned, non-overlapping 3×3 blocks. Create one output cell per block, so an H×W input maps to an (H/3)×(W/3) output. Within each block, ignore colors 0 and 5; output the most frequent remaining color, or 0 if none remain. Demonstrations confirm 12×12→4×4, 18×18→6×6, and 21×21→7×7; the 24×24 test was solved as 8×8 using this rule. Count colors separately within each 3×3 block. Do not aggregate across 6×6 regions or whole panels.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T13:06:15.808Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T13:39:10.520Z","version":3},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682203/attempts/5aeabceef638470ab98c0ce83fca400e/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
