{"id":"refine_20260929140008184","summary":"Updated the existing global horizontal-gap memory with a grid-dimension validation lesson from task-729ad7fe.","rationale":"The trajectory confirms the established one-cell horizontal gap-fill rule, while the first submission was rejected because one output row had the wrong length; the corrected grid solved the task. An existing global memory already covers this rule, so updating it avoids a duplicate.","expectedOutcome":"Future solvers can apply the gap-fill rule and verify every output row matches the input width before submission.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_fill_single_cell_gaps_between_horizontal_markers_task_9a0028f5","title":"ARC: fill single-cell horizontal gaps between markers","content":"In a uniform-background grid, when same-row marker pixels are separated by exactly one background cell (columns c and c+2), recolor only the intervening cell to color 2. Preserve markers and all other cells; do not extend filling beyond the gap. Evidence includes task-729ad7fe: background-6 grids with color-1 markers (and a demo with color-8 markers) follow this rule. Before submitting, validate that the output has the intended number of rows and that every row has the original width; an otherwise plausible first attempt failed because one row was malformed.","path":"arc_tasks","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Preserve the confirmed rule while adding a directly observed, broadly useful output-shape validation lesson.","before":{"id":"arc_fill_single_cell_gaps_between_horizontal_markers_task_9a0028f5","kind":"memory","title":"ARC: fill single-cell horizontal gaps between markers","content":"In a uniform-background grid, when same-row marker pixels are separated by exactly one background cell (columns c and c+2), recolor only the intervening cell to color 2. Preserve markers and all other cells; do not extend filling beyond the final marker. Confirmed for task-9a0028f5 and task-729ad7fe acr