{"id":"refine_20260929142910117","summary":"Updated the task-790052e7 memory with the confirmed divider-panel rule and the correction that output 2 marks aligned background cells in both panels.","rationale":"The solved test and demonstrations support comparing aligned cells across equal-sized panels: output 2 where both cells are their respective backgrounds, and 0 wherever either panel has a mark. Earlier submissions show that reversing the output encoding or using only one panel’s marks leads to errors.","expectedOutcome":"Future solvers can identify the panels, compare their background-versus-mark status cell by cell, and validate the output dimensions and 2/0 encoding against the demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_790052e7_intersect_divider_separated_binary_panels","title":"Task-790052e7: aligned panel backgrounds map to 2; union of marks maps to 0","content":"For task-790052e7, a full straight divider separates two equal-sized panels, horizontally or vertically. Compare aligned cells. Output has the dimensions of one panel: write 2 when BOTH cells are their respective panels' uniform background colors; otherwise write 0. Equivalently, identify non-background marks in each panel and write 0 at the union of their aligned positions, with 2 everywhere else. Panel background and mark colors can differ. Do not invert this encoding: the output background is 2, not 0, and marks from either panel force 0. Validate the panel split, alignment, dimensions, and encoding against the demonstrations.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"Captures the confirmed task rule and directly addresses the failed attempts that used a reversed encoding or considered only one panel's marks.","before":{"id":"arc_task_790052e7_intersect_divider_separated_binary_panels","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-790052e7: intersect divider-separated binary panels","content":"Validated on task-790052e7. Input is a grid split into two equal-sized pane