{"id":"refine_20260929154602339","summary":"Updated the global task-250f69a6 memory with the validated motif-replication rule and center alignment.","rationale":"The task was solved after demonstrations showed the motif copied at isolated marker positions; the final test output confirmed center-cell alignment for the 3×3 motif and preservation of the original.","expectedOutcome":"On recurrence, solvers should identify the motif and markers, place one motif copy centered on each marker, preserve the source and background, and check clipping at grid edges.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_250f69a6_replicate_three_cell_line_at_markers","title":"ARC task-250f69a6: replicate the multicolor motif at marker centers","content":"For task-250f69a6, identify the compact multicolor motif against the uniform background and the isolated marker pixels elsewhere. Replicate the motif once at each marker, aligning the marker with the center cell of the motif's bounding box. For an odd-sized 3×3 motif, place its top-left at (marker_row−1, marker_col−1). Preserve the original motif and background; copy only motif-colored cells, overlaying them at each placement and clipping any cells beyond the grid. Demos validated this for different backgrounds, motif colors, and marker colors. In the solved test, the background was 4, the marker pixels were 0, and the motif was [[8,8,2],[.,9,2],[.,9,9]]; the resulting output was confirmed correct. A 1×5 demo motif was aligned by its center column. Do not infer marker color from the background: identify the isolated repeated marker color in each instance.","path":"arc_tasks","metadata":{"scope":"global","evidence":"Three demonstrations and a correctly solved test"},"reason":"Preserves the validated placement rule and clarifies how center alignment, marker color, source preservation, and edge clipping apply.","before":{"id":"arc_task_250f69a6_replicate_three_cell_line_at_markers","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-250f