{"id":"refine_20260929154711981","summary":"Updated the global task-8adf9d3b memory with the validated four-rotation quadrant rule.","rationale":"The 4×4 demonstration and accepted 8×8 test confirm that an n×n input becomes a 2n×2n grid: upper-left is unchanged, upper-right is rotated 90° clockwise, lower-left 90° counterclockwise, and lower-right 180°. The earlier incorrect submission came from assembling the rotations incorrectly, not from an incorrect rule.","expectedOutcome":"Future solvers can construct each quadrant independently, validate the 2n×2n dimensions and rotation directions, and avoid repeating the assembly error.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_doubled_noisy_grid_task_8adf9d3b_observations","title":"ARC task-8adf9d3b: doubled grid of rotated input quadrants (validated)","content":"Confirmed rule for task-8adf9d3b: for an n×n input, produce a 2n×2n output composed of four n×n quadrants. Place the original input unchanged in the upper-left; its 90° clockwise rotation in the upper-right; its 90° counterclockwise rotation in the lower-left; and its 180° rotation in the lower-right. This is confirmed by the 4×4 demonstration and an accepted 8×8 test. Build each transformed quadrant independently, then place it at the corresponding output offset; check dimensions and rotation directions before submitting. The earlier incorrect attempt resulted from incorrectly assembling the rotations, not from an incorrect transformation rule.","metadata":{"scope":"global"},"reason":"The prior memory described the remaining quadrants as unresolved, but the trajectory now validates their exact arrangement and records the cause of the earlier failed submission.","before":{"id":"arc_doubled_noisy_grid_task_8adf9d3b_observations","kind":"memory","title":"ARC doubled noisy grid task-8adf9d3b: quadrant histogram and unresolved layouts","content":"Confirmed from four demonstrations (input dimensions 14x14, 12x12, 8x8, 9x9): an n×n input maps to a 2n×2n output. The upper-left n×n quadrant is an exact copy of the input. Each output quadrant has the same color histogram (cell counts by color) as the input. The other three quadrants contain different arrangements of the same multiset; no simple copy, tiling, rotation/reflection, sorted arrangement, or random-shuffle guess was validated. A test on 8x8 requiring 16x16 was exhausted with eight incorrect outputs, including repeated input tiling, independent random shuffles matching histograms, and other arrangements. Exact placements appear unconstrained/random from demonstrations, so do not claim a solved deterministic placement rule. If task recurs, construct the correct 2n×2n dimensions, preserve input in upper-left, and ensure all other quadrants reproduce the input histogram, but recognize exact-match scoring cannot be assured without finding additional placement logic.","path":"arc_tasks","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:59:13.551577+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T15:43:36.338140+00:00","version":6},"after":{"id":"arc_doubled_noisy_grid_task_8adf9d3b_observations","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-8adf9d3b: doubled grid of rotated input quadrants (validated)","content":"Confirmed rule for task-8adf9d3b: for an n×n input, produce a 2n×2n output composed of four n×n quadrants. Place the original input unchanged in the upper-left; its 90° clockwise rotation in the upper-right; its 90° counterclockwise rotation in the lower-left; and its 180° rotation in the lower-right. This is confirmed by the 4×4 demonstration and an accepted 8×8 test. Build each transformed quadrant independently, then place it at the corresponding output offset; check dimensions and rotation directions before submitting. The earlier incorrect attempt resulted from incorrectly assembling the rotations, not from an incorrect transformation rule.","path":"arc_tasks","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global"},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-09-29T12:59:13.551577+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-29T15:47:18.522Z","version":7},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1790682203/attempts/5aeabceef638470ab98c0ce83fca400e/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
